  "lastName": "Ballmann",
  "overview": "I am a well-versed scientist in both basic and applied techniques with an emphasis on physiological and psychophysiological responses to exercise, physiology of music, ergogenic aids, and sport/exercise performance. My primary research focus is related to using music as a means to improve physical ability and psychophysiological responses to exercise in both athletes and clinical populations. Additionally, I investigate nutritional supplementation as a means to improve exercise performance in athletes and recreational exercisers with a special emphasis on sympathomimetics and stimulants. I am passionate about mentoring students through research experiences. I believe music and exercise are the best medicine. I am a Fellow of the American College of Sports Medicine.",
